# Moonstone, Harsh Mistress: "you may exile that card from your graveyard. If you do, until the end of your next turn, you may play
# that card." Faithless Looting discards a Lightning Bolt and a Forest on turn 1: the Bolt's exile is accepted and the Forest's
# declined, so the Forest stays in the graveyard. The Bolt may be played until the end of Bot1's next turn (turn 3) and no longer:
# on turn 5, with the red mana for it in the pool, it can't be cast from exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Moonstone, Harsh Mistress
Faithless Looting
Lightning Bolt
Forest
Swamp x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Moonstone, Harsh Mistress.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt; Forest)
Bot1.Decline
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
? Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Forest
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)

[Expect]
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Forest
